**What changed:** The Angular language service (`NgLanguageService`, `@angular/language-service`) gained a new public API method `ensureProjectAnalyzed(): void`, which "Triggers the Angular compiler's analysis pipeline without performing per-file type checking. This is a lighter alternative to calling `getSemanticDiagnostics()` when the goal is only to ensure that the Angular project has been analyzed (e.g. during project initialization)" (`packages/language-service/api.ts`). The implementation in `LanguageService.ensureProjectAnalyzed()` calls `compiler.getTemplateTypeChecker()` via `withCompilerAndPerfTracing(PerfPhase.LsDiagnostics, ...)`, forcing Angular compiler analysis/resolution through the public compiler API without computing per-file diagnostics; the method is also exposed from the TS plugin factory `create()` in `packages/language-service/src/ts_plugin.ts` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/39f62fa40805c60b2d0dd44bae960ec8fc39764f.patch, cherry-picked as https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/d2137928e8f075527016a3c011dd8efc4d4e1ebd). The VS Code extension server startup path (`vscode-ng-language-service/server/src/session.ts`) now calls `languageService.ensureProjectAnalyzed()` (guarded by `isNgLanguageService(...)`) instead of `project.getLanguageService().getSemanticDiagnostics(fileName)` on the first root script, since the per-file diagnostics results "were never consumed"; the debug trace label changed from `Global analysis - getSemanticDiagnostics for <fileName>` to `Global analysis - ensureProjectAnalyzed for <projectName>`.

